INT. COUNTY COURTHOUSE - STAIRWELL LANDING - DAY

Marble. Echo. A broken radiator ticking.

ATTORNEY SIMONE BELLAMY-OKONKWO (30s, charcoal suit, briefcase like a shield) paces. Phone to ear. Voicemail again.

Across the landing, her client DARNELL "DEE" PRUITT (20s, borrowed tie, handcuffs hidden under a jacket draped over his wrists) sits on a bench, jaw tight. A bailiff, BAILIFF OSEI TEMPLETON (50s, belly, patience), stands guard.

SIMONE
Pick up, Judge. Pick up.

DEE
He's not going to pick up.

SIMONE
Be quiet and memorize your answers.

DEE
I did.

SIMONE
Again.

DEE
I was home at nine. My cousin brought the pizza. My cousin is gone now.

SIMONE
Gone where?

DEE
Gone gone.

Simone hangs up. Stares at him. The radiator clanks. Templeton shifts his weight, glances at his watch, clears his throat, then looks at the ceiling as if to give them privacy.

The stairwell door slams open. Footsteps below, fast, then up.

DISTRICT ATTORNEY PRUDHOMME LACROIX (50s, silver hair, voice like warm gravel) arrives on the landing with a file under his arm. He stops. Smiles at no one in particular.

LACROIX
Counsel. A word.

SIMONE
Not without a witness.

LACROIX
The bailiff is a witness.

TEMPLETON
I'm furniture, sir.

LACROIX
We have a recording from the pizza shop.

Dee goes rigid. Simone doesn't move. Lacroix slides a tablet out of his file, taps it, holds it up. Grainy footage: a delivery counter, a man in a hoodie, a timestamp at 9:14.

SIMONE
That's not my client.

LACROIX
Isn't it?

Dee lunges up from the bench. The jacket slips. The cuffs flash. Templeton catches his elbow and Simone puts a hand flat on Dee's chest. Lacroix steps back, the tablet falling, clattering down the marble steps.

SIMONE
Sit down. Now.

Dee sits. Breathing hard. Simone turns to Lacroix.

SIMONE (CONT'D)
That footage has no chain of custody.

LACROIX
Then why did he flinch?

SIMONE
Because you're standing six inches from his face, Prudhomme.

A pause. Lacroix retrieves the tablet from the stairs with a wince at the cracked screen, tucks it away, and exhales.

LACROIX
Plea's still on the table. Ten minutes.

He exits. Templeton sighs.

TEMPLETON
Never seen a man look so pleased about a broken screen.

Simone sits next to Dee. For the first time, she lets her shoulders drop.
